■ Rules on Issuance of Various Certificates by National Schools, etc. [Attached Table] [Amended on April 12, 2023]

Types of Certificates Issued by Schools (Related to Article 2 (1))

1. Schools falling under Article 2, subparagraph 2, of the Early Childhood Education Act:
(a) Certificate of enrollment;
(b) Certificate of graduation;
(c) Certificate of kindergarten life records;
(d) Certificate of payment of education expenses.

2. Schools falling under Article 2 of the Elementary and Secondary Education Act:
(a) Certificate of enrollment;
(b) Transcript of academic records (excluding elementary schools and equivalent schools);
(c) Certificate of school life records;
(d) Certificate of removal from the school register (or management outside the prescribed student quota);
(e) Certificate of graduation (or expected graduation);
(f) Certificate of payment of education expenses.

3. Schools falling under Article 2 of the Higher Education Act:
(a) Certificate of enrollment;
(b) Transcript of academic records;
(c) Certificate of academic register;
(d) Certificate of removal from the school register;
(e) Certificate of graduation (or expected graduation);
(f) Certificate of admission examination success;
(g) Certificate of admission;
(h) Certificate of leave of absence;
(i) Certificate of reinstatement;
(j) Certificate of voluntary withdrawal;
(k) Certificate of completion (or expected completion);
(l) Certificate of degree conferment (or expected conferment);
(m) Certificate of completion (or expected completion) of a double major;
(n) Certificate of completion (or expected completion) of a minor;
(o) Certificate of payment of education expenses;
(p) Certificate of completion (or expected completion) of a teacher education course;
(q) Certificate of work experience as an instructor.
